 {
  "id": "s09",
  "start": 43.11,
  "props": {
   "kind": "claudeResponse",
   "prompt": "Remove the \"Do you have pets?\" question from the booking form.",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "text": "I'll find the booking form in your app folder and remove that question.",
     "gap": 0
    },
    {
     "text": "I've removed the pets question from the booking form. The change is saved in your app folder but not committed to git.",
     "gap": 22
    },
    {
     "text": "**`index.html`:** the \"Do you have pets?\" Yes/No block is gone.",
     "bullet": true,
     "gap": 16
    },
    {
     "text": "**`js/booking.js`:** the form no longer sends `has_pets`, which would break once the question is gone. The `has_pets` column already allows blank values, so the database needs no change. New bookings will save it as unknown.",
     "bullet": true
    },
    {
     "text": "**The catch: pet homes can go to cat-allergic cleaners.** The rest of the app still uses the pets answer:",
     "gap": 22
    },
    {
     "text": "Auto-assign in `js/matching.js` keeps homes with pets away from cleaners with a cat allergy. With no answer, it treats every new booking as pet-free, so it could send a cleaner with a cat allergy to a home that has pets.",
     "bullet": true,
     "gap": 16
    },
    {
     "text": "The staff page will show \"No\" in the Pets column. It also won't show the \"Needs pet-friendly cleaner\" badge.",
     "bullet": true
    },
    {
     "text": "Staff can still set pets by hand with the edit checkbox on each booking.",
     "bullet": true
    }
   ],
   "streamStart": 0.1,
   "streamDur": 1.6,
   "hl": [
