 {
  "id": "s49",
  "start": 300.01,
  "props": {
   "kind": "prompt",
   "label": "Paste this prompt",
   "title": "Prompt 1 · Map it",
   "body": "Before changing anything: list every file, query, type, component, test, email template and API call that reads, writes or displays `has_pets` (also search for `hasPets`, `pets` and `pet_`). For each one, tell me what happens for new records where the value is null. Then tell me what you could NOT check, such as database functions, triggers or third-party services. Don't edit anything yet.",
   "cps": 140,
   "size": 32,
   "dur": 13.9
  }
 },
 {
  "id": "s50",
  "start": 313.89,
  "props": {
   "kind": "prompt",
   "label": "Run this in the Supabase SQL editor",
   "title": "Prompt 2 · The blast-radius query",
   "body": "-- views that use the column (tracked by Postgres)\nselect 'view' as kind, view_schema::text as schema, view_name::text as name\nfrom information_schema.view_column_usage\nwhere table_schema = 'public' and table_name = 'bookings' and column_name = 'has_pets'\n\nunion all\n\n-- functions whose body mentions it (bodies are NOT dependency-tracked, so search the text)\nselect 'function', n.nspname::text, p.proname::text\nfrom pg_proc p\njoin pg_namespace n on n.oid = p.pronamespace\nwhere p.prosrc ilike '%has_pets%'\n  and n.nspname not in ('pg_catalog', 'information_schema')\n\nunion all\n\n-- RLS policies whose expressions mention it\nselect 'policy', schemaname::text, (tablename || '.' || policyname)::text\nfrom pg_policies\nwhere qual ilike '%has_pets%' or with_check ilike '%has_pets%'\n\nunion all\n\n-- every user trigger on the table (check what each function does)\nselect 'trigger on bookings', 'public', (t.tgname || ' -> ' || t.tgfoid::regproc::text)\nfrom pg_trigger t\nwhere t.tgrelid = 'public.bookings'::regclass and not t.tgisinternal\n\norder by 1, 3;",
   "cps": 300,
   "size": 18,
   "note": "Full query in the description",
   "dur": 12.733333333333333
  }
 },
 {
  "id": "s51",
  "start": 326.64,
  "props": {
   "kind": "prompt",
   "label": "Paste this prompt",
   "title": "Prompt 3 · Make it safe",
   "body": "We're removing the \"[question]\" question from the form. Existing records keep their value. New records store null, which means \"unknown\", not \"no\". Before removing the input, update every place that reads `[column]` so that null shows \"Unknown\", is flagged for a person to confirm, and never gets the \"no\" behaviour automatically. Then remove the input. Don't drop the column. Show me each change.",
   "cps": 140,
   "size": 32,
   "dur": 14.3
  }
 },
